<title>SPAIN: Spain Feb CPI fell 0.1 pct vs Jan, up 2.5 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Spain Feb CPI fell 0.1 pct vs Jan, up 2.5 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute (INE) gave the following figures:</p>
<p> SPANISH INFLATION		FEB 97    JAN 97   FEB 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index change     -0.1	 0.3	 0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 2.5	 2.9	 3.7</p>
<p> Core inflation		    0.1	 0.2	 0.6</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 2.3	 2.8	 4.2</p>
<p> INDEX BY COMPONENTS	     FEB 97     JAN 97     YR/YR</p>
<p> Food				  -0.8	  0.2	 1.3</p>
<p> Clothing			     0.0	  0.1	 2.2</p>
<p> Housing				0.2	  0.1	 3.8</p>
<p> Household goods		    0.3	  0.2	 2.8</p>
<p> Medicine			     0.8	  0.7	 3.5</p>
<p> Transport			    0.1	  0.7	 3.0</p>
<p> Culture				0.2	  0.2	 2.1</p>
<p> Other				  0.3	  0.4	 3.5</p>
<p>Note - In food, fresh food fell 1.3 pct from the previous month (up 2.6 pct year-on-year) and processed food fell 0.4 pct (up 0.5 pct year-on-year)</p>
</text>
